    note: 'The floor is low because global gig platforms put Indian freelancers in direct price competition with designers worldwide. The ceiling is genuinely open for designers who build a specific niche, case-study proof, and repeat clients instead of competing purely on price.',
  },
];

const flatRows = [
  {
    signal: 'A portfolio of 3-5 near-identical case studies: a food-delivery app redesign, a fitness app redesign, a to-do list app, all following the exact same bootcamp template',
    reality: "Recruiters and hiring managers report that more than 90% of junior UI/UX portfolios now look almost identical, because most bootcamp graduates work through the same handful of practice-project templates. A portfolio that only shows this kind of output is competing against hundreds of visually similar submissions for the same junior opening, not against a handful of genuinely different candidates.",
  },
  {
    signal: 'A short paid bootcamp completed mainly to \"break into tech fast\" with no real client, startup, or nonprofit project behind it',
